# pygments-kleio

Pygments lexer for **Kleio notation**, the source-transcription language
of the [Timelink](https://github.com/time-link) system for historical
research.

Registers the `kleio` (and `cli`) alias with Pygments via entry points,
so once installed, any tool using Pygments — MkDocs, MkDocs Material,
Sphinx, `pygmentize` — can highlight ` ```kleio ` code fences and
`.kleio` / `.cli` / `.rpt` files.

## Install

```bash
pip install ./pygments-kleio          # vendored here, for the docs build
# or, from the standalone home of the grammar:
pip install git+https://github.com/time-link/pygments-kleio.git
```

## Test

```bash
pygmentize -l kleio example.cli
```

## Origin

Ported from the TextMate grammar
[time-link/kleio-grammar](https://github.com/time-link/kleio-grammar)
(`source.kleio`) and from `prism-kleio`, with two fixes: correct
`A-Za-z` character ranges (the originals had the classic `A-z` leak) and
underscores allowed in group/element names (e.g. `/place_of_burial=`).

MIT licensed; see `LICENSE`.
